# MED-MT83-ACE (Livia), MT8385. Not final: unreleased, V0.1 layout.
#
# CON1, from the board's ODB++ (MED-MT83-ACE-V0.1-20251205): each header pin's
# net, traced to the SoC ball it reaches; Name is the ball's GPIO<n>, Desc its
# alternate functions in mode order 1-7 (MT8385 datasheet, as the docs repo's
# SoC ball DB carries it). Chip 0 is pinctrl_paris (192 lines, legacy sysfs
# base 512, measured on this board), so Line is n and sysfs is 512+n.
#
# Pins 8, 10, 12, 35, 38, 40 reach the SoC through a series resistor on the
# CON1 side (R145, R144, R146, R149, R147, R148 in that order); Ref is the
# header-side net. Pins 2/4 are EX_DTB_POWER, the 5 V Type-C VBUS through R3
# (0 R) -- the schematic, not the layout, states the voltage.
#rpi-header: CON1
